closed	p2	SA effective-round resolution isn't Cancelled-aware — VP diverges from GW/TP on a soft-cancelled round. resolve_sa_effective_rounds (engine/src/tournament/sanctions.rs:42) seated_in closure (:48-54) tests seating membership without filtering Cancelled tables. Consumers then diverge: sa_vp_penalty (:96) subtracts 1 VP per resolved SA independent of table iteration, while table_sa_adjustments (GW/TP) is invoked per-table by update_standings which skips Cancelled tables first (standings.rs:47,322) — so an SA whose effective round is soft-cancelled applies the VP penalty but NOT the GW/TP penalty. Trigger: an SA resolves onto a soft-cancelled parallel round (stored points there, or the (0..nrounds).rev().find(seated_in) fallback picks it because the player last appears in the cancelled round). Silent; violates the doc invariant at sanctions.rs:39-41 / assert :93 (effective round is a real played round); corrupts standings + finals seeding. Fix (same shape as count_played_rounds): make seated_in require a non-Cancelled table. relates:#362
