closed	p2	Tournament start/finish were stored tz-aware by three writers, breaking the naive-wall-clock+timezone convention (organizer report: VEKN event showing 07:00 instead of 09:00). CONVENTION (now in ARCHITECTURE.md 'API & Data Conventions'): start/finish are NAIVE, paired with the separate Tournament.timezone field, never tz-aware - readers anchor the wall clock in that zone (routes/calendar._as_utc, frontend utils.zonedDate), so a stored instant gets shifted by the venue offset a second time. Old archon uses the same convention (it indexes on (start || ' ' || timezone)::timestamptz, and dump values carry no offset). VIOLATORS FIXED: (1) vekn_tournament_sync._parse_date converted VEKN's venue wall clock to UTC (commit 62fc225) - now writes it verbatim and only fills timezone from the venue guess; (2) routes/tournaments.py stamped finish=datetime.now(UTC) on Finished in both the /action and offline-sync paths - now _wall_clock_now(tournament.timezone); (3) migrate_from_archon.parse_dt forced tzinfo=UTC onto legacy naive values, so every migrated tournament read back shifted by its venue offset - new parse_wall_dt for start/finish (parse_dt still used for instants: modified/deleted_at/issued_at). SELF-HEAL: vekn-linked rows correct themselves on the next sync run (start/finish are in both change comparisons), legacy-only rows on the next nightly merge. NOT self-healing: finish values already stamped aware UTC on tournaments finished in-app before this fix - no writer rewrites them. Hence backend/scripts/normalize_wall_clock.py: rewrites any stored start/finish that still carries an offset as the wall clock in the tournament's own timezone, report by default, --apply to write, idempotent. It is a CUTOVER STEP (#40 and .pst/details/35, phase 2): run after the final legacy merge + VEKN sync so the self-healing writers go first, and before the ratings recompute since a rating's date is finish-or-start and a shifted instant lands on the wrong day at the edges. Verified on the dev DB: 8187 rows in 24s, second run reports 0, all three access projections carry the naive value. Also fixed en route: the config form is fed by ConfigTab's start.slice(0,16), which drops the offset - that was how the aware value surfaced as a 2h-early time in a disabled field, and saving any config field would have written it back as the real start. Regression test test_vekn_tournament_sync.py::test_import_stores_naive_wall_clock_paired_with_timezone. Side effect: the sync/native start skew the name+start-within-24h adoption key works around (VEKN_SYNC.md) loses its systematic component. INGEST BELT (added after review): routes/tournaments.py normalizes client-supplied start/finish at every whole-object ingest - create_tournament, the /action config path, and both offline-sync paths - via _normalize_wall_clock/_wall_clock. An offset is CONVERTED to the tournament timezone, never truncated: truncating would move the event by the difference between the sender's zone and the venue's. No client sends one today (datetime-local posts naive text and nothing in the tournament frontend passes start/finish through Date/toISOString), but these endpoints decode whole Tournament objects off the wire, so the convention is enforced at the boundary rather than assumed.
