closed	p2	List filters survive Back (#533 put them in the URL) but not the nav menu: clicking Tournaments/Rankings/Community in the sidebar or bottom bar is a bare href, so currentParams() reads nothing and the viewer lands on the unfiltered default. User pushed back that Back-only persistence is not what was asked. RESEARCH (2026-08-04, Pencil&Paper enterprise filtering, Aufait dashboard filter guide, Smart Interface Design Patterns, NN/g faceted search): persistence is the DEFAULT expectation in data-heavy tools; the documented mitigation for the surprise-state risk is not to skip persistence but to make the applied state conspicuous (visible control values + applied-filter summary + one-click clear). Recommended architecture is layered: URL canonical (done) + short-lived per-tab session memory for in-app navigation + explicit saved views (out of scope). PLAN: (1) new lib/last-view.ts - syncQueryParams mirrors the query string into sessionStorage per route key with a timestamp; layout derives navItems hrefs as route+remembered search, so the URL stays the single source of truth with no mount-time replaceState and no flash of unfiltered content (navItems at routes/+layout.svelte:38 feeds both navs, one change point; also the logo link :222). (2) sessionStorage not localStorage - per-tab, dies with the tab, so a shared link or fresh open is always clean; plus a ~30min inactivity TTL because a PWA tab can live for days on mobile. (3) do NOT remember page (position, not preference - entry resets to page 1; Back still restores it from the URL) and do NOT remember q (a free-text query is an intent; a restored one makes the list look broken). Remember state/country/format/online/roles/tab. (4) view=agenda|all moves to localStorage - it is a display preference like the theme, and must not fight the default-to-agenda-once-auth-resolves effect at tournaments/+page.svelte:56. (5) empty states must say no-results-for-these-filters with a clear-filters action, not no-tournaments - this is the main mitigation for a restored filter that hides data (state=finished, online=false). (6) clear the memory on logout: stateOptions drops finished for anonymous viewers (tournaments/+page.svelte:96) so a stale param would select a nonexistent option. SURFACES: routes/tournaments/+page.svelte, routes/rankings/+page.svelte, lib/components/UserList.svelte - all already routed through lib/url-filters.ts. relates:#533 relates:#532
